## QuestionsFormTextProvider

Context-based DI provider for text resolution. Wrap `QuestionsForm` with this provider to supply i18n / translation logic. All child components (`SelectQuestion`, `SelectQuestionOption`, `InputQuestion`, `AutocompleteQuestion`) resolve text via the `useResolveText()` hook — no prop drilling. For rich secondary content (e.g. colored option subtitles) use the `useResolveNode()` hook, which uses the resolver's optional `resolveNode` and falls back to `resolveText`.

### QuestionsFormTextResolver Interface

| Method        | Signature                                  | Description                                                                                                   |
| ------------- | ------------------------------------------ | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `resolveText` | `(text: string \| undefined) => string`    | Resolves text keys to display text                                                                            |
| `resolveNode` | `(text: string \| undefined) => ReactNode` | Optional. Resolves a key to rich inline nodes (e.g. colored segments) for option subtitles. Falls back to `resolveText` when omitted. |

### Usage

```tsx
import { QuestionsFormTextProvider, type QuestionsFormTextResolver } from 'etoro-ui/questions-form';

class MyTextResolver implements QuestionsFormTextResolver {
  resolveText(text: string | undefined): string {
    if (!text) return '';
    return i18n.t(text) ?? text;
  }
}

const resolver = new MyTextResolver();

<QuestionsFormTextProvider resolver={resolver}>
  <QuestionsForm config={config}>
    <QuestionsForm.Submit onSubmit={handleSubmit} />
  </QuestionsForm>
</QuestionsFormTextProvider>;
```

If no external provider is wrapped, QuestionsForm creates one internally from `config.textAsKeys` / `config.getText` for backward compatibility.

